{"ts": "2026-11-10T05:10:49+00:00", "move": "critique", "round": 1, "summary": {"attacks": [], "dropped": [], "absence_unverified": [], "needed_evidence": ["TfL August 2023 ULEZ expansion charging scheme order, boundary map and vehicle guidance: establish the M25 exclusion and applicable specialist-vehicle categories, weight limits and exemptions. These details are needed to resolve the existing reading objections to C4.", "LAQN and Defra AURN ratified hourly NO2 data and station metadata for outer-London roadside monitors, 29 August 2022–28 August 2024: identify a fixed panel within the newly charged area and calculate equally weighted before-and-after annual means, data completeness and site-specific changes.", "London-wide ULEZ One Year Report, Appendix 3, Table 70 and underlying analysis data/code: obtain every monthly expansion-only contrast and an estimate specifically averaged over 29 August 2023–28 August 2024. Establish how the smoothed, changing-monitor zonal estimates relate to the fixed-panel annual estimand rather than treating September 2024's 4.8% as the annual effect.", "London-wide ULEZ One Year Report, Appendix 3, 'Estimating impact uncertainties using Bootstrap', pages 185–194: retrieve numerical confidence bounds specifically for the No London-wide ULEZ contrast, in µg/m³ and percentage terms. Seek uncertainty for the annual average and sensitivity to counterfactual specification, not the all-phase No ULEZ intervals in Table 67.", "London-wide ULEZ One Year Report counterfactual validation, pages 169–177, and supporting technical files: seek outer-London versus 5–40 km control-zone pre-trend comparisons, placebo interventions, alternative controls and quantified sensitivity to expansion spillovers into control roadside and background sites. Establish whether subtracting and adding the observed control background preserves expansion-mediated effects.", "London-wide ULEZ One Year Report analysis separating the expansion from concurrent bus electrification, taxi/private-hire requirements and other transport policies: seek an expansion-only concentration contrast that retains changes those policies would have produced without expansion, while retaining changes induced by expansion. The joint attribution described on page 60 does not itself provide this separation.", "Outer-London NO2 meteorological-normalisation and background-trend decomposition for 29 August 2023–28 August 2024 versus the preceding twelve months: seek quantified weather, regional-background and natural-fleet-turnover contributions, with uncertainty, rather than general statements that these determinants matter.", "Further improvement in London's air quality demands more, Figure 3, Supplementary Tables S5–S6 and Figure S7: retrieve outer-London traffic-site ULEZ3 NO2 effect estimates and numerical uncertainty bounds, counterfactual training dates and treatment of anticipatory changes. Search for an updated analysis extending beyond 30 April 2024 through 28 August 2024; the reported non-significant short-period result cannot establish an exact annual null.", "London-wide ULEZ One Year Report site-level concentration results and monitoring inventory for its 29 outer-London roadside NO2 sites: seek spatially disaggregated expansion-only effects, site inclusion histories and weighting or representativeness analysis supporting generalisation from monitored roads to the newly covered outer-London area."]}, "state_hash": "a5bca3fbb696d12857f0c333384a4cc175c3fe552c0600fd8145778610cadeec", "prev_hash": "65ed8ae3c164ea54cc77ca9730c3d53089313605dad856b73367eb64320e759e", "usage": [{"provider": "openai", "model": "gpt-6-astra", "input_tokens": 26982, "output_tokens": 1613, "role": "critic"}], "hash": "667c26888faae3d5272b3bfe3031e072890b4d2458f75a2df282862177231345"}
