{"ts": "2026-11-10T05:22:47+00:00", "move": "critique", "round": 2, "summary": {"attacks": [], "dropped": [], "absence_unverified": [], "needed_evidence": ["LAQN, AURN and borough monitoring archives: obtain ratified hourly NO2 data and site-location histories for roadside monitors within the newly covered ULEZ area, covering 29 August 2022–28 August 2024. Identify a fixed, comparable panel and calculate equally weighted before-and-after means in µg/m³, percentage changes and site-level variation.", "London-wide ULEZ One Year Report, Appendix 3, Table 70 (p. 192), underlying data and replication code: obtain the complete monthly observed and 'No London-wide ULEZ' concentration series. Seek an expansion-only mean effect for 29 August 2023–28 August 2024, rather than treating the September 2024 endpoint reduction of 1.1 µg/m³ (4.8%) as the first-year average.", "London-wide ULEZ One Year Report, Appendix 3, bootstrap analysis (pp. 185–188): locate numerical 95% intervals for the paired expansion-only concentration difference and its annual average. Table 67's all-ULEZ uncertainty is not interchangeable with uncertainty against continuation of the pre-existing ULEZ.", "London-wide ULEZ One Year Report, counterfactual methodology and limitations (pp. 169–177): obtain pre-expansion treatment–control trend diagnostics and quantitative sensitivity tests for contamination of the 5–40 km control zone, different fleet composition, alternative controls and the December 2022 starting point. Check how subtraction and restoration of control-zone background concentrations handles expansion-induced background changes.", "London-wide ULEZ One Year Report, attribution scope (p. 60) and limitations (pp. 175–176): seek a concentration-effect decomposition or sensitivity analysis separating the expansion from bus electrification, taxi and private-hire licensing changes that would have occurred without it, while retaining expansion-induced scrappage, anticipatory replacement and associated transport changes.", "Further improvement in London's air quality demands more…, Figure 3, Supplementary Tables S5–S6 and Figure S7: extract outer-London traffic-site NO2 effect estimates, numerical uncertainty intervals, donor weights and pre-treatment fit diagnostics. Compare these with the official estimates over the same first-three-month window; seek a replication extended through 28 August 2024. Non-significance over the shorter window does not establish an exactly zero full-year effect."]}, "state_hash": "0d2868c2fb7859e38efc1867807e6d0776981d72a0226ec7099729e59eeeeccb", "prev_hash": "7cb94edd06e74e2855aa5b09afb90153a27689ab9ae46d9815216c080adbe5bb", "usage": [{"provider": "openai", "model": "gpt-6-astra", "input_tokens": 41227, "output_tokens": 1550, "role": "critic"}], "hash": "8670eb5abed39d38ad7682e20511757afa77ce81736c1218c5babf308f84ce05"}
